1
00:00:01,819 --> 00:00:09,619
Chapter 14 For several subsequent days I saw little of Mr. Rochester.

2
00:00:10,819 --> 00:00:15,959
In the mornings he seemed much engaged with business, and in the afternoon

3
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:19,116
gentleman from Milcott or the neighborhood

4
00:00:19,116 --> 00:00:21,720
called, and sometimes stayed to dine with him.

5
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:27,700
When his sprain was well enough to admit of horse exercise, he rode out a good

6
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:32,819
deal, probably to return these visits, as he generally did not come back.

7
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:33,919
Till late at night.

8
00:00:35,279 --> 00:00:40,020
During this interval, even Adele was seldom sent for to his presence,

9
00:00:40,889 --> 00:00:44,740
and all my acquaintance with him was confined to an occasional wrong contrary

10
00:00:44,741 --> 00:00:50,479
in the hall, on the stairs, or in the gallery, when he would sometimes pass me

11
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:55,759
haughtily and coldly, just acknowledging my presence by a distant nord or a cool

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:01:00,700
glance, and sometimes bow and smile with gentleman-like affability.

13
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:05,444
His changes of mood did not offend me, because I

14
00:01:05,445 --> 00:01:08,080
saw that I had nothing to do with their alternation.

15
00:01:08,759 --> 00:01:13,619
The air been flow depended on causes quite disconnected with me.

16
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:20,020
One day, he had had company to dinner, and had sent for my portfolio,

17
00:01:20,779 --> 00:01:23,959
in order, doubtless, to exhibit its contents.

18
00:01:24,979 --> 00:01:28,340
The gentleman went away early to attend a public meeting at Milcott.

19
00:01:28,669 --> 00:01:33,165
As Mrs Fairfax informed me, but the night being wet

20
00:01:33,166 --> 00:01:37,119
and inclement, Mr. Rochester did not accompany them.

21
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:40,680
Soon after they were gone, he rang the bell.

22
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:44,759
A message came that I and Adele were to go downstairs.

23
00:01:45,849 --> 00:01:51,180
I brushed Adele's hair and made her neat, and having ascertained that I was myself

24
00:01:51,181 --> 00:01:57,380
in my usual quaker trim, where there was nothing to retouch, all being too close

25
00:01:57,381 --> 00:02:02,060
and plain, braided locks included, to admit of disarrangement.

26
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,700
We descended.

27
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,880
Adele wondering whether the pity cough ray

28
00:02:06,881 --> 00:02:10,320
was at length come, for owing to some mistake.

29
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:12,740
Its arrival had hitherto been delayed.

30
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,520
She was gratified.

31
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:20,119
There it stood, a little carton on the table when we entered the dining room.

32
00:02:21,049 --> 00:02:23,139
She appeared to know it by instinct.

33
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:27,479
Ma boite, ma boite exclaimed she, running towards it.

34
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,459
Yes, there is your boite at last.

35
00:02:32,599 --> 00:02:35,664
Take it into a corner, you genuine daughter of

36
00:02:35,665 --> 00:02:38,720
Paris, and amuse yourself with disemboweling it.

37
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:44,500
Said the deep and rather sarcastic voice of Mr. Rochester, proceeding from the

38
00:02:44,501 --> 00:02:47,500
depths of an immense easy chair at the fireside.

39
00:02:48,659 --> 00:02:54,840
And mind, he continued, don't bother me with any details of the anatomical

40
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:58,799
process, or any notice of the condition of the entrails.

41
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:02,159
Let your operation be conducted in silence.

42
00:03:03,279 --> 00:03:06,939
Tien's toire tranquille en font comprenne -tout.

43
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:10,959
Adele seemed scarcely to need the warning.

44
00:03:11,939 --> 00:03:15,197
She had already retired to a sofa with her treasure,

45
00:03:15,198 --> 00:03:18,240
and was busy untying the cord which secured the lid.

46
00:03:19,389 --> 00:03:23,659
Having removed this impediment, and lifted certain silvery envelopes of

47
00:03:23,661 --> 00:03:28,568
tissue paper, she merely exclaimed, oh, siel, kuke boe,

48
00:03:28,569 --> 00:03:33,020
and then remained absorbed in ecstatic contemplation.

49
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:35,520
Is Miss Eyre there?

50
00:03:36,459 --> 00:03:40,919
Now demanded the master, half rising from his seat to look round to the door,

51
00:03:41,319 --> 00:03:42,759
near which I still stood.

52
00:03:43,279 --> 00:03:45,959
Ah, well, come forward, be seated here.

53
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:48,540
He drew a chair near his own.

54
00:03:50,049 --> 00:03:53,919
I am not fond of the prattle of children, he continued.

55
00:03:55,560 --> 00:04:01,800
For all bachelor as I am, I have no pleasant associations connected with their lisp.

56
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:07,299
It would be intolerable to me to pass a whole evening, tet-a-tet with a brat.

57
00:04:08,625 --> 00:04:10,840
Don't draw that chair farther off Miss Eyre.

58
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,060
Sit down exactly where I placed it.

59
00:04:14,845 --> 00:04:18,159
If you please, that is, confound these civilities.

60
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,060
I continually forget them.

61
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,520
Nor do I particularly affect simple-minded old ladies.

62
00:04:25,819 --> 00:04:28,680
By the by, I must have mine in mind.

63
00:04:29,279 --> 00:04:30,619
It won't do to neglect her.

64
00:04:31,159 --> 00:04:33,040
She is a fairfax or wet to one.

65
00:04:33,759 --> 00:04:35,959
And blood is said to be thicker than water.

66
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:42,040
He rang, and dispatched an invitation to Mrs Fairfax, who soon arrived,

67
00:04:42,639 --> 00:04:43,759
knitting basket in hand.

68
00:04:44,705 --> 00:04:45,705
Good evening, madam.

69
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,479
I send to you for a charitable purpose.

70
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:52,575
I have forbidden Adele to talk to me about her

71
00:04:52,576 --> 00:04:55,980
presence, and she is bursting with repulsion.

72
00:04:56,299 --> 00:05:00,319
Have the goodness to serve her as auditress and interlocutress.

73
00:05:00,919 --> 00:05:04,880
It will be one of the most benevolent acts you ever performed.

74
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:12,099
Adele, indeed, no sooner saw Mrs Fairfax, than she summoned her to her sofa,

75
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:15,682
and there quickly filled her lap with the porcelain,

76
00:05:15,683 --> 00:05:18,460
the ivory, the wax and contents of her boite.

77
00:05:19,799 --> 00:05:23,743
Pooring out meantime, explanations and raptures

78
00:05:23,744 --> 00:05:27,501
in such broken English as she was mistress of.

79
00:05:28,659 --> 00:05:34,619
Now I have performed the part of a good host, pursued Mr. Rochester, put my guests

80
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:37,227
into the way of amusing each other, I ought

81
00:05:37,228 --> 00:05:40,280
to be at liberty to attend to my own pleasure.

82
00:05:41,490 --> 00:05:45,619
Mr. Air, draw your chair still a little farther forward.

83
00:05:46,479 --> 00:05:47,880
You are yet too far back.

84
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:52,680
I cannot see you without disturbing my position in this comfortable chair,

85
00:05:53,389 --> 00:05:55,520
which I have no mind to do.

86
00:05:57,159 --> 00:06:03,241
I did, as I was bid, though I would much rather have remained somewhat in the shade.

87
00:06:03,799 --> 00:06:07,880
But Mr. Rochester had such a direct way of giving orders.

88
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:11,520
It seemed a matter of course to obey him promptly.

89
00:06:13,169 --> 00:06:16,299
We were, as I have said, in the dining room.

90
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:19,866
The luster, which had been lit for dinner,

91
00:06:19,866 --> 00:06:23,841
filled the room with a festal breadth of light.

92
00:06:24,229 --> 00:06:26,919
The large fire was all red and clear.

93
00:06:27,659 --> 00:06:32,540
The purple curtains hung rich and ample before the lofty window and lofty arch.

94
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:37,220
Everything was still, saved the subdued chat of a del.

95
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,340
She dared not speak loud.

96
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:45,159
And filling up each pause, the beating of winter rain against the pains.

97
00:06:46,919 --> 00:06:51,110
Mr. Rochester, as he sat in his damace -covered chair,

98
00:06:51,111 --> 00:06:53,841
looked different to what I had seen him look before.

99
00:06:54,819 --> 00:06:57,439
Not quite so stern, much less gloomy.

100
00:06:58,639 --> 00:07:03,400
There was a smile on his lips and his eyes sparkled, whether with wine or not,

101
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,779
I am not sure, but I think it very probable.

102
00:07:07,750 --> 00:07:13,619
He was, in short, in his after-dinner mood, more expanded and genial and also

103
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:17,000
more self-indulgent than the frigid and rigid temper of the morning.

104
00:07:17,939 --> 00:07:23,439
Still, he looked preciously grim, cushioning his massive head against the

105
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:26,691
swelling back of his chair and receiving the light of the

106
00:07:26,692 --> 00:07:31,900
fire on his granite-hune features, and in his great dark eyes.

107
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:37,779
For he had great dark eyes and very fine eyes, too.

108
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:43,180
Not without a certain change in their depth, sometimes which, if it was not

109
00:07:43,181 --> 00:07:47,180
softness, reminded you at least of that feeling.

110
00:07:49,029 --> 00:07:51,973
He had been looking two minutes at the fire, and

111
00:07:51,973 --> 00:07:54,840
I had been looking the same length of time at him.

112
00:07:55,459 --> 00:08:00,479
When turning suddenly, he caught my gaze fastened on his physiognomy.

113
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,459
You examine me, Miss Eyre, said he.

114
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,580
Do you think me handsome?

115
00:08:07,409 --> 00:08:12,159
I should, if I had deliberated, have replied to this question by something

116
00:08:12,161 --> 00:08:14,978
conventionally vague and polite, but the answer

117
00:08:14,979 --> 00:08:17,279
somehow slipped from my tongue before I was aware.

118
00:08:18,599 --> 00:08:19,599
No, sir.

119
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,099
Ah, buy my word.

120
00:08:22,845 --> 00:08:25,560
There is something singular about you, said he.

121
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:32,919
You have the air of a little non-net, quaint, quiet, grave and simple,

122
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:37,700
as you sit with your hands before you and your eyes generally bent on the carpet,

123
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:44,919
except by the by, when they are directed piercingly to my face, as just now,

124
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,060
for instance.

125
00:08:46,799 --> 00:08:51,119
And when one asks you a question, or makes a remark to which you are obliged

126
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:58,599
to reply, you wrap out a round rejoinder, which, if not blunt, is at least brusque.

127
00:08:59,599 --> 00:09:01,459
What do you mean by it, sir?

128
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:04,759
I was too plain, I beg your pardon.

129
00:09:05,970 --> 00:09:08,706
I ought to have replied that it was not easy to give

130
00:09:08,707 --> 00:09:11,540
an impromptu answer to a question about appearances.

131
00:09:12,759 --> 00:09:15,851
That tastes mostly differ, and that beauty is

132
00:09:15,852 --> 00:09:19,580
of little consequence or something of that sort.

133
00:09:20,500 --> 00:09:25,319
You ought to have replied no such thing, beauty of little consequence indeed,

134
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:29,948
and so under pretense of softening the previous

135
00:09:29,949 --> 00:09:34,000
outrage, of stroking and soothing me into placidity.

136
00:09:34,959 --> 00:09:37,099
You stick a sly pen knife under my ear.

137
00:09:37,639 --> 00:09:38,639
Go on.

138
00:09:39,069 --> 00:09:40,919
What fault do you find with me, prey?

139
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:45,560
I suppose I have all my limbs and all my features like any other man.

140
00:09:47,159 --> 00:09:51,099
Mr. Rochester, allow me to disown my first answer.

141
00:09:51,959 --> 00:09:54,040
I intended no pointed repartee.

142
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,680
It was only a blunder.

143
00:09:56,340 --> 00:09:57,340
Just so.

144
00:09:57,799 --> 00:10:00,740
I think so, and you shall be answerable for it.

145
00:10:01,599 --> 00:10:02,599
Criticize me.

146
00:10:02,799 --> 00:10:04,080
Does my forehead not please you?

147
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:10,119
He lifted up the sable waves of hair which lay horizontally over his brow and showed

148
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:16,099
a solid enough mass of intellectual organs, but an abrupt deficiency where the

149
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:18,740
suave sign of benevolence should have risen.

150
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,799
Now, ma'am, am I a fool?

151
00:10:23,979 --> 00:10:27,529
Far from it, sir, you would perhaps think me rude if

152
00:10:27,530 --> 00:10:30,720
I inquired in return whether you are a philanthropist?

153
00:10:31,639 --> 00:10:37,939
There again another stick of the pen knife when she pretended to pat my head.

154
00:10:38,889 --> 00:10:44,240
And that is because I said I did not like the society of children and old women,

155
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:45,880
lobe it spoken.

156
00:10:47,090 --> 00:10:53,200
No young lady, I am not a general philanthropist, but I bear a conscience.

157
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:58,919
And he pointed to the prominences which are said to indicate that faculty,

158
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:04,560
and which, fortunately for him, was sufficiently conspicuous, giving

159
00:11:04,561 --> 00:11:08,200
indeed a marked breadth to the upper part of his head.

160
00:11:09,599 --> 00:11:13,939
And besides, I once had a kind of rude tenderness of heart.

161
00:11:15,055 --> 00:11:21,240
When I was as old as you, I was a feeling fellow enough, partial to the unfledged,

162
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:25,340
unfostored, and unlucky, but fortune has knocked me about since.

163
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:31,259
She has even needed me with her knuckles, and now I flatter myself I am hard and

164
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:35,599
tough as an India rubber ball, pervious though through a chink or two

165
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:39,099
still, and with one sentient point in the middle of the lump.

166
00:11:39,979 --> 00:11:42,799
Yes, does that leave hope for me?

167
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:45,220
Hope of what, sir?

168
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:50,659
Of my final retransformation from India, rubber back to flesh?

169
00:11:52,299 --> 00:11:55,200
Decidedly, he has had too much wine, I thought.

170
00:11:56,569 --> 00:12:00,479
And I did not know what answer to make to his queer question.

171
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:05,459
How could I tell whether he was capable of being retransformed?

172
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:12,319
You looked very much puzzled, Miss Eyre, and though you are not pretty any more

173
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:16,020
than I am handsome, yet a puzzled air becomes you.

174
00:12:17,235 --> 00:12:22,919
Besides, it is convenient, for it keeps those searching eyes of yours away from my

175
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:29,020
physiognomy, and bizzies them with the worsted flowers of the rug, so puzzle on.

176
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:35,340
Young lady, I am disposed to be gregarious and communicative tonight.

177
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:41,115
With this announcement, he rose from his chair and

178
00:12:41,116 --> 00:12:44,380
stood, leaning his arm on the marble mantelpiece.

179
00:12:45,319 --> 00:12:49,599
In that attitude, his shape was seen plainly as well as his face.

180
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:56,361
His unusual breadth of chest disproportionate almost to his length of limb.

181
00:12:56,639 --> 00:13:01,759
I am sure most people would have thought him an ugly man, yet there was so much

182
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:08,080
unconscious pride in his port, so much ease in his demeanor, such a look

183
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:14,639
of complete indifference to his own external appearance, so haughty a reliance

184
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:20,639
on the power of other qualities intrinsic or adventitious to atone for the lack of

185
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:27,340
mere personal attractiveness, that in looking at him, one inevitably shared the

186
00:13:27,341 --> 00:13:33,920
indifference, and even in a blind imperfect sense put faith in the confidence.

187
00:13:35,279 --> 00:13:40,680
I am disposed to be gregarious and communicative tonight, he repeated,

188
00:13:41,599 --> 00:13:43,220
and that is why I sent for you.

189
00:13:43,959 --> 00:13:47,616
The fire and the chandelier were not sufficient company for

190
00:13:47,617 --> 00:13:51,240
me, nor would Pylor have been, for none of these can talk.

191
00:13:52,419 --> 00:13:55,680
A del is a degree better but still far below the mark.

192
00:13:56,819 --> 00:14:01,639
Mrs. Fairfax Ditto, you, I am persuaded, can suit me if you will.

193
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:05,580
You puzzled me the first evening I invited you down here.

194
00:14:06,779 --> 00:14:08,799
I have almost forgotten you since.

195
00:14:09,939 --> 00:14:14,439
Other ideas have driven yours from my head, but tonight I am resolved to be at

196
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:18,599
ease, to dismiss what importunes and recall what pleases.

197
00:14:19,709 --> 00:14:24,759
It would please me now to draw you out, to learn more of you, therefore speak.

198
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:31,901
Instead of speaking, I smiled, and not a very complacent or submissive smile, either.

199
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,540
Speak, he urged.

200
00:14:34,159 --> 00:14:35,159
What about, sir?

201
00:14:35,729 --> 00:14:38,278
Whatever you like, I leave both the choice of subject

202
00:14:38,279 --> 00:14:40,681
and the manner of treating it entirely to yourself.

203
00:14:41,959 --> 00:14:44,119
Accordingly, I sat and said nothing.

204
00:14:45,625 --> 00:14:51,020
If he expects me to talk for the mere sake of talking and showing off, he will find

205
00:14:51,021 --> 00:14:54,139
he has addressed himself to the wrong person, I thought.

206
00:14:55,119 --> 00:14:56,560
You are dumb, miss air.

207
00:14:57,599 --> 00:14:58,700
I was dumb still.

208
00:15:00,259 --> 00:15:02,898
He bent his head a little towards me, and with a

209
00:15:02,899 --> 00:15:05,560
single hasty glance seemed to dive into my eyes.

210
00:15:06,619 --> 00:15:09,180
Stubborn, he said, and annoyed.

211
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,180
Ah, it is consistent.

212
00:15:11,930 --> 00:15:14,880
I put my request in an absurd, almost insolent form.

213
00:15:15,819 --> 00:15:16,939
Miss air, I beg your pardon.

214
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:22,060
The fact is, once for all, I don't wish to treat you like an inferior.

215
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,139
That is, correcting himself.

216
00:15:26,270 --> 00:15:30,125
I claim only such superiority as must result from 20 years

217
00:15:30,126 --> 00:15:33,520
difference in age and a century's advance in experience.

218
00:15:34,459 --> 00:15:38,619
This is legitimate, at JTNs, as Adele would say.

219
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:43,459
And it is by virtue of this superiority and this alone.

220
00:15:44,459 --> 00:15:48,720
That I desire you to have the goodness to talk to me a little now, and divert my

221
00:15:48,721 --> 00:15:54,180
thoughts, which are galled with dwelling on one point, cankering as a rusty nail.

222
00:15:56,549 --> 00:16:01,819
He had dainned an explanation, almost an apology, and I did not feel

223
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:05,080
insensible to his condescension and would not sign so.

224
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:09,580
I am willing to amuse you if I can, sir, quite willing.

225
00:16:10,369 --> 00:16:16,080
But I cannot introduce a topic, because how do I know what will interest you?

226
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:19,979
Ask me questions, and I will do my best to answer them.

227
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:26,759
Then, in the first place, do you agree with me that I have a right to be a little

228
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:33,700
masterful, abrupt, perhaps exacting sometimes, on the grounds I stated,

229
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:40,680
namely, that I am old enough to be your father, and that I have battled through a

230
00:16:40,681 --> 00:16:46,560
varied experience with many men of many nations, and roamed over half the globe

231
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:50,520
while you have lived quietly with one set of people in one house.

232
00:16:51,619 --> 00:16:57,799
Do as you please, sir, that is no answer, or rather it is a very irritating,

233
00:16:58,569 --> 00:17:01,439
because a very evasive one reply clearly.

234
00:17:03,264 --> 00:17:08,560
I don't think, sir, you have a right to come on me, merely because you are older

235
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:12,200
than I, or because you have seen more of the world than I have.

236
00:17:13,069 --> 00:17:15,717
Your claim to superiority depends on the use

237
00:17:15,718 --> 00:17:18,701
you have made of your time and experience.

238
00:17:19,979 --> 00:17:21,939
Hmpf, promptly spoken.

239
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:27,599
But I won't allow that, seeing that it would never suit my case as I have made an

240
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:31,619
indifferent, not to say a bad use of both advantages.

241
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:38,439
Leaving superiority out of the question then, you must still agree to receive my

242
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:43,540
orders now and then, without being peaked or hurt by the tone of command.

243
00:17:44,319 --> 00:17:45,319
Will you?

244
00:17:45,939 --> 00:17:46,939
I smiled.

245
00:17:47,830 --> 00:17:50,299
I thought to myself Mr. Rochester is peculiar.

246
00:17:51,450 --> 00:17:55,619
He seems to forget that he pays me £30 per annum for receiving his orders.

247
00:17:57,270 --> 00:18:01,900
The smile is very well, said he, catching instantly the passing expression,

248
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:03,740
but speak too.

249
00:18:05,139 --> 00:18:10,479
I was thinking, sir, that very few masters would trouble themselves to inquire

250
00:18:10,904 --> 00:18:15,220
whether or not their paid subordinates were peaked and hurt by their orders.

251
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:17,619
Payed subordinates?

252
00:18:18,139 --> 00:18:19,139
What?

253
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,060
You are my paid subordinate, are you?

254
00:18:21,619 --> 00:18:23,360
Oh, yes, I'd forgotten the salary.

255
00:18:24,349 --> 00:18:29,299
Well then, on that mercenary ground, will you agree to let me hector a little?

256
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:36,000
No, sir, not on that ground, but on the ground that you did forget it,

257
00:18:36,639 --> 00:18:38,917
and that you care whether or not a dependent is

258
00:18:38,918 --> 00:18:42,680
comfortable in his dependency, I agree heartily.

259
00:18:44,029 --> 00:18:48,560
And will you consent to dispense with the great many conventional forms and phrases

260
00:18:48,561 --> 00:18:54,979
without thinking that the omission arises from insolence?

261
00:18:56,560 --> 00:19:02,580
I am sure, sir, I should never mistake informality for insolence, one I rather

262
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:08,259
like, the other nothing free-born would submit to even for a salary.

263
00:19:09,849 --> 00:19:14,819
Humbug, most things free-born will submit to anything for a salary.

264
00:19:15,619 --> 00:19:18,878
Therefore, keep to yourself and don't venture on

265
00:19:18,879 --> 00:19:22,360
generalities of which you are intensely ignorant.

266
00:19:23,860 --> 00:19:30,200
However, I mentally shake hands with you for your answer, despite its inaccuracy,

267
00:19:31,479 --> 00:19:36,500
and as much for the manner in which it was said, as for the substance of the speech,

268
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:38,799
the manner was frank and sincere.

269
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:41,799
One does not often see such a manner.

270
00:19:42,819 --> 00:19:48,540
No, on the contrary, affectation or coldness or stupid, course-minded

271
00:19:48,541 --> 00:19:53,659
misapprehension of one's meaning are the usual rewards of candor.

272
00:19:54,919 --> 00:19:59,439
Not three in three thousand raw school -girl governesses would have answered me

273
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:03,220
as you have just done, but I don't mean to flatter you.

274
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:08,740
If you are cast in a different mold to the majority, it is no merit of yours.

275
00:20:09,659 --> 00:20:15,119
Nature did it, and then, after all, I go too fast in my conclusions.

276
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:18,799
For what I yet know, you may be no better than the rest.

277
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:22,700
You may have intolerable defects to counterbalance your few good points.

278
00:20:22,701 --> 00:20:26,060
And so may you, I thought.

279
00:20:26,909 --> 00:20:30,259
My eye met his, as the idea crossed my mind.

280
00:20:31,029 --> 00:20:33,526
He seemed to read the glance, answering as if

281
00:20:33,527 --> 00:20:36,901
its import had been spoken as well as imagined.

282
00:20:37,709 --> 00:20:40,479
Yes, yes, you are right," said he.

283
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:42,720
I have plenty of faults of my own.

284
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:47,500
I know it, and I don't wish to palliate them, I assure you.

285
00:20:48,930 --> 00:20:51,299
God would I need not be too severe about others.

286
00:20:52,279 --> 00:20:57,580
I have a past existence, a series of deeds, a color of life to contemplate

287
00:20:57,580 --> 00:21:00,575
within my own breast, which might well call my

288
00:21:00,576 --> 00:21:03,279
snares and censures from my neighbours to myself.

289
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:10,360
I started, or rather, for like other defaulters, I like to lay half the blame

290
00:21:10,361 --> 00:21:17,520
on ill fortune and adverse circumstances, was thrust onto a wrong tack at the age of

291
00:21:17,521 --> 00:21:22,080
one and twenty, and have never recovered the right cause since.

292
00:21:23,415 --> 00:21:24,895
But I might have been very different.

293
00:21:25,639 --> 00:21:30,080
I might have been as good as you, wiser, almost astainless.

294
00:21:30,869 --> 00:21:36,760
I envy you, your peace of mind, your clean conscience, your unpiluted memory.

295
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:42,599
Little girl, a memory without blot or contamination must be an exquisite

296
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:47,599
treasure, an inexhaustible source of pure refreshment, is it not?

297
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,380
How was your memory when you were eighteen, sir?

298
00:21:52,509 --> 00:21:55,279
All right then, limpid, salubrius?

299
00:21:56,220 --> 00:21:59,080
No gush of bilge water had turned it to fetid puddle.

300
00:22:00,270 --> 00:22:03,900
I was your equal at eighteen, quite your equal.

301
00:22:05,159 --> 00:22:08,646
Nature meant me to be, on the whole, a good man, miss

302
00:22:08,647 --> 00:22:13,020
air, one of the better kind, and you see I am not so.

303
00:22:14,380 --> 00:22:15,959
You would say you don't see it.

304
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:21,360
At least I flatter myself, I read as much in your eye, beware by the by what you

305
00:22:21,361 --> 00:22:24,700
express with that organ I am quick at interpreting its language.

306
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:28,040
Then take my word for it.

307
00:22:29,110 --> 00:22:34,819
I am not a villain, you are not to suppose that, not to attribute to me any such bad

308
00:22:34,820 --> 00:22:37,842
eminence, but owing I verily believe, rather

309
00:22:37,843 --> 00:22:41,681
to circumstances than to my natural bent.

310
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:46,639
I am a trite commonplace sinner, hackneyed in all the poor petty

311
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:51,540
dissipations, with which the rich and worthless tried to put on life.

312
00:22:52,639 --> 00:22:54,740
Do you wonder that I avow this to you?

313
00:22:56,319 --> 00:23:01,540
Know that in the course of your future life, you will often find yourself elected

314
00:23:01,541 --> 00:23:05,479
the involuntary confidant of your acquaintances' secrets.

315
00:23:06,729 --> 00:23:12,180
People will instinctively find out, as I have done, that it is not your forte

316
00:23:12,181 --> 00:23:16,959
to tell of yourself, but to listen while others talk of themselves.

317
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:24,139
They will feel, too, that you listen with no malevolent scorn of their indiscretion,

318
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:27,200
but with a kind of innate sympathy.

319
00:23:28,049 --> 00:23:30,669
Not the less comforting and encouraging, because

320
00:23:30,669 --> 00:23:33,341
it is very unobtrusive in its manifestations.

321
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:35,500
How do you know?

322
00:23:36,349 --> 00:23:37,840
How can you guess all this, sir?

323
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,040
I know it well.

324
00:23:40,939 --> 00:23:46,639
Therefore, I proceed almost as freely as if I were writing my thoughts in a diary.

325
00:23:47,709 --> 00:23:52,400
You would say, I should have been superior to circumstances, so I should,

326
00:23:52,770 --> 00:23:55,479
so I should, but you see, I was not.

327
00:23:57,110 --> 00:24:00,860
When fate wronged me, I had not the wisdom to remain cool.

328
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,840
I turned desperate.

329
00:24:03,759 --> 00:24:04,819
Then I degenerated.

330
00:24:05,729 --> 00:24:11,840
Now, when any vicious simpleton excites my disgust by his poultry, ribaldry,

331
00:24:12,689 --> 00:24:14,939
I cannot flatter myself that I am better than he.

332
00:24:15,750 --> 00:24:18,419
I am forced to confess that he and I are on a level.

333
00:24:19,159 --> 00:24:20,400
I wish I had stood firm.

334
00:24:21,119 --> 00:24:22,119
God knows I do.

335
00:24:23,319 --> 00:24:25,799
Dred remorse when you attempted to err, Missiah.

336
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:28,439
Remorse is the poison of life.

337
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:32,459
Repentance is said to be its cure, sir.

338
00:24:33,490 --> 00:24:34,520
It is not its cure.

339
00:24:35,279 --> 00:24:38,180
Reformation may be its cure, and I could reform.

340
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:40,139
I have strength yet for that.

341
00:24:40,985 --> 00:24:43,779
If, but where is the use of thinking of it?

342
00:24:44,459 --> 00:24:46,880
Hampered, burdened, cursed as I am.

343
00:24:48,049 --> 00:24:51,591
Besides, since happiness is irrevocably denied me, I have

344
00:24:51,592 --> 00:24:55,599
a right to get pleasure out of life, and I will get it.

345
00:24:55,939 --> 00:24:56,939
Cost what it may.

346
00:24:58,319 --> 00:25:00,119
Then you will degenerate still more, sir.

347
00:25:01,340 --> 00:25:05,959
Possibly, yet why should I, if I can get sweet fresh pleasure?

348
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:11,599
And I may get it as sweet and fresh as the wild honey the bee gathers on the more.

349
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:14,240
It will sting.

350
00:25:14,919 --> 00:25:16,400
It will taste bitter, sir.

351
00:25:17,819 --> 00:25:18,819
How do you know?

352
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:21,200
You never tried it.

353
00:25:22,259 --> 00:25:23,659
How very serious.

354
00:25:24,970 --> 00:25:30,459
How very solemn you look, and you are as ignorant of the matter as this cameo head,

355
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,720
taking one from the mantelpiece.

356
00:25:33,990 --> 00:25:38,479
You have no right to preach to me, you neophyte, that have not passed the

357
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:43,400
porch of life, and are absolutely unequainted with its mysteries.

358
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:46,959
I only remind you of your own words, sir.

359
00:25:47,799 --> 00:25:53,201
You said error brought remorse, and you pronounced remorse the poison of existence.

360
00:25:53,790 --> 00:25:55,259
And who talks of error now?

361
00:25:56,040 --> 00:25:59,659
I scarcely think the notion that flittered across my brain was an error.

362
00:26:00,099 --> 00:26:04,099
I believe it was an inspiration, rather than a temptation.

363
00:26:05,119 --> 00:26:07,439
It was very genial, very soothing.

364
00:26:08,020 --> 00:26:09,020
I know that.

365
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:10,500
Here it comes again.

366
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:14,223
It is no devil I assure you, or if it be, it

367
00:26:14,223 --> 00:26:17,980
has put on the robes of an angel of light.

368
00:26:18,319 --> 00:26:22,740
I think I must admit so fair a guest, when it asks entrance to my heart.

369
00:26:24,220 --> 00:26:27,580
Distrusted, sir, it is not a true angel.

370
00:26:28,779 --> 00:26:30,419
Once more, how do you know?

371
00:26:31,630 --> 00:26:35,959
By what instinct do you pretend to distinguish between a fallen serif of the

372
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:42,319
abyss and a messenger from the eternal throne, between a guide and a seducer?

373
00:26:43,860 --> 00:26:47,509
I judged by your countenance, sir, which was troubled

374
00:26:47,510 --> 00:26:50,400
when you said the suggestion had returned upon you.

375
00:26:51,189 --> 00:26:54,959
I feel sure it will work you more misery if you listen to it.

376
00:26:56,110 --> 00:26:57,110
Not at all.

377
00:26:57,720 --> 00:27:00,080
It bears the most gracious message in the world.

378
00:27:01,130 --> 00:27:05,479
For the rest, you are not my conscience keeper, so don't make yourself uneasy.

379
00:27:05,939 --> 00:27:08,540
Here, come in, Bonnie Wanderer.

380
00:27:10,020 --> 00:27:14,220
He said this as if he spoke to a vision, viewless to any eye but his own.

381
00:27:15,189 --> 00:27:20,720
Then, folding his arms, which he had half extended on his chest, he seemed to

382
00:27:20,721 --> 00:27:23,240
enclose in their embrace the invisible being.

383
00:27:24,919 --> 00:27:31,259
Now, he continued again addressing me, I have received the pilgrim, a disguised

384
00:27:31,260 --> 00:27:34,939
deity as I verily believe, already it has done me good.

385
00:27:35,979 --> 00:27:39,200
My heart was a sort of channel, it will now be a shrine.

386
00:27:41,150 --> 00:27:44,099
To speak truth, sir, I don't understand you at all.

387
00:27:45,369 --> 00:27:48,659
I cannot keep up the conversation because it has got out of my depth.

388
00:27:49,849 --> 00:27:54,840
Only one thing I know, you said you were not as good as you should like to be,

389
00:27:55,819 --> 00:27:58,599
and that you regretted your own imperfection.

390
00:27:59,779 --> 00:28:01,520
One thing I can comprehend.

391
00:28:03,060 --> 00:28:07,580
You intimated that to have a sullied memory was a perpetual bane.

392
00:28:08,770 --> 00:28:13,939
It seems to me that if you tried hard, you would in time find it possible to

393
00:28:13,940 --> 00:28:19,639
become what you yourself would approve, and that if from this day you began with

394
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:22,419
resolution to correct your thoughts and actions.

395
00:28:23,290 --> 00:28:28,799
You would in a few years have laid up a new and stainless store of recollections,

396
00:28:29,299 --> 00:28:32,060
to which you might revert with pleasure.

397
00:28:33,639 --> 00:28:37,144
Justly thought rightly said Messiah, and at

398
00:28:37,145 --> 00:28:41,659
this moment I am paving hell with energy, sir.

399
00:28:42,970 --> 00:28:46,560
I am laying down good intentions which I believe durable as flint.

400
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:51,919
Certainly, my associates and pursuits shall be other than they have been,

401
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:54,700
and better, and better.

402
00:28:55,520 --> 00:28:58,400
So much better as pure awe is than foul draws.

403
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,000
You seem to doubt me.

404
00:29:00,159 --> 00:29:01,159
I don't doubt myself.

405
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:07,419
I know what my aim is, what my motives are, and at this moment I pass a law,

406
00:29:08,099 --> 00:29:12,139
unalterable as that of the Medis and Persians, that both are right.

407
00:29:13,610 --> 00:29:17,099
They cannot be sir if they require a new statute to legalize them.

408
00:29:18,689 --> 00:29:23,439
They are, miss air, though they absolutely require a new statute.

409
00:29:24,360 --> 00:29:28,680
Unheard of combinations of circumstances demand unheard of rules.

410
00:29:30,049 --> 00:29:32,245
That sounds a dangerous maxim, sir, because

411
00:29:32,246 --> 00:29:34,959
one can see at once that it is liable to abuse.

412
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:38,400
Sententious sage, so it is.

413
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:41,720
But I swear by my household gods not to abuse it.

414
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:44,319
You are human and fallible.

415
00:29:44,959 --> 00:29:45,459
I am.

416
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:46,900
So are you.

417
00:29:47,299 --> 00:29:48,299
What then?

418
00:29:48,459 --> 00:29:50,880
The human and fallible should not irrigate a power with

419
00:29:50,881 --> 00:29:55,180
which the divine and perfect alone can be safely entrusted.

420
00:29:56,439 --> 00:29:57,439
What power?

421
00:29:58,110 --> 00:30:04,161
That of saying, of any strange unsanctioned line of action, let it be right.

422
00:30:04,990 --> 00:30:05,990
Let it be right.

423
00:30:06,439 --> 00:30:08,959
The very words you have pronounced them.

424
00:30:10,560 --> 00:30:14,579
May it be right then, I said, as I rose, deeming it useless

425
00:30:14,580 --> 00:30:17,880
to continue a discourse which was all darkness to me.

426
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:23,939
And besides, sensible that the character of my interlocutor was beyond my

427
00:30:23,940 --> 00:30:27,139
penetration, at least beyond its present reach.

428
00:30:28,180 --> 00:30:31,633
And feeling the uncertainty, the vague sense of

429
00:30:31,633 --> 00:30:34,779
insecurity which accompanies a conviction of ignorance.

430
00:30:36,909 --> 00:30:37,909
Where are you going?

431
00:30:38,819 --> 00:30:41,400
To put a del to bed, it is past her bedtime.

432
00:30:42,950 --> 00:30:45,540
You are afraid of me because I talk like a sphinx.

433
00:30:46,610 --> 00:30:48,380
Your language is enigmatical, sir.

434
00:30:49,220 --> 00:30:52,840
But though I am bewildered, I am certainly not afraid.

435
00:30:53,990 --> 00:30:54,990
You are afraid.

436
00:30:55,439 --> 00:30:56,840
Your self-love dreads a blunder.

437
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,900
In that sense, I do feel apprehensive.

438
00:31:02,060 --> 00:31:03,860
I have no wish to talk nonsense.

439
00:31:05,500 --> 00:31:12,861
If you did, it would be in such a grave, quiet manner, I should mistake it for sense.

440
00:31:13,380 --> 00:31:14,759
Do you never laugh, miss air?

441
00:31:15,599 --> 00:31:17,380
Don't trouble yourself to answer.

442
00:31:18,310 --> 00:31:22,540
I see you laugh rarely, but you can laugh very merrily.

443
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:28,020
Believe me, you are not naturally austere, any more than I am naturally vicious.

444
00:31:29,369 --> 00:31:34,319
The low wood constraint still clings to you somewhat, controlling your features,

445
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:38,020
muffling your voice, and restricting your limbs.

446
00:31:38,904 --> 00:31:43,500
And you fear in the presence of a man and a brother, or father, or master,

447
00:31:43,819 --> 00:31:49,959
or what you will, to smile too galley, speak too freely, or move too quickly.

448
00:31:51,029 --> 00:31:55,663
But in time, I think you will learn to be natural with

449
00:31:55,664 --> 00:31:59,180
me, as I find it impossible to be conventional with you.

450
00:32:00,159 --> 00:32:02,965
And then your looks and movements will have more

451
00:32:02,966 --> 00:32:05,780
vivacity and variety than they dare offer now.

452
00:32:07,290 --> 00:32:10,329
I see it intervals, the glance of a curious sort

453
00:32:10,353 --> 00:32:13,240
of bird through the close set bars of a cage.

454
00:32:13,779 --> 00:32:17,319
A vivid, restless, resolute captive is there.

455
00:32:18,110 --> 00:32:19,259
Were it but free?

456
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:21,220
It would soar cloud high.

457
00:32:22,450 --> 00:32:23,840
You are still bent on going.

458
00:32:25,424 --> 00:32:26,840
It has struck nine, sir.

459
00:32:27,779 --> 00:32:28,779
Never mind.

460
00:32:29,220 --> 00:32:30,220
Wait a minute.

461
00:32:30,319 --> 00:32:31,799
A del is not ready to go to bed yet.

462
00:32:32,599 --> 00:32:35,259
My position, miss air, with my back to the fire

463
00:32:35,260 --> 00:32:38,241
and my face to the room, favours observation.

464
00:32:39,099 --> 00:32:44,279
While talking to you, I have also occasionally watched a del.

465
00:32:44,849 --> 00:32:49,060
I have my own reasons for thinking her a curious study, reasons that I may,

466
00:32:49,599 --> 00:32:52,200
nay that I shall impart to you some day.

467
00:32:53,549 --> 00:32:57,819
She pulled out of her box about ten minutes ago, a little pink silk frock,

468
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:00,740
wrapped a lit her face as she unfolded it.

469
00:33:01,619 --> 00:33:04,322
Coquetry runs in her blood, blends with her

470
00:33:04,323 --> 00:33:08,080
brains, and seasons the marrow of her bones.

471
00:33:10,125 --> 00:33:13,779
Ylfoca Julesse cried, she, et a lint storm mim.

472
00:33:15,319 --> 00:33:16,680
And she rushed out of the room.

473
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:20,939
She is now with Sufi, undergoing a robing process.

474
00:33:21,900 --> 00:33:23,860
In a few minutes, she will reenter.

475
00:33:24,779 --> 00:33:30,240
And I know what I shall see, a miniature of Celine Varan, as she used to appear on

476
00:33:30,241 --> 00:33:33,500
the boards at the rising of... but never mind that.

477
00:33:34,549 --> 00:33:39,119
However, my tenderest feelings are a bout to receive a shock.

478
00:33:39,860 --> 00:33:41,319
Such is my presentiment.

479
00:33:41,919 --> 00:33:44,779
Stay now, to see whether it will be realized.

480
00:33:45,900 --> 00:33:49,840
Erlong, Adele's little foot was heard tripping across the hall.

481
00:33:50,599 --> 00:33:54,500
She entered, transformed as her guardian had predicted.

482
00:33:55,540 --> 00:33:59,000
A dress of rose-colored satin, very short.

483
00:33:59,790 --> 00:34:03,487
And as full in the skirt as it could be gathered,

484
00:34:03,488 --> 00:34:06,800
replaced the brown frock she had previously worn.

485
00:34:07,630 --> 00:34:10,159
A wreath of rose-budds circled her forehead.

486
00:34:10,900 --> 00:34:14,779
Her feet were dressed in silk stockings and small white satin sandals.

487
00:34:16,209 --> 00:34:21,599
Esset que marob va bien, cried she, bounding forwards, aimé sou liés,

488
00:34:22,220 --> 00:34:25,720
aimé bas, tenez, je crois que je vais danser.

489
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:31,939
And spreading out her dress, she chasse across the room till, having reached Mr.

490
00:34:32,139 --> 00:34:33,139
Rocheste.

491
00:34:33,220 --> 00:34:36,403
She wheeled lightly round before him, on tiptoe,

492
00:34:36,404 --> 00:34:40,139
then dropped on one knee at his feet, exclaiming.

493
00:34:46,750 --> 00:34:51,599
Then rising she added, ses comcelles que m 'amont faisait, n'est-ce pas monsieur,

494
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:56,299
précise-les was the answer, and comcelle.

495
00:34:57,150 --> 00:35:01,419
She charmed my English gold out of my British British pocket.

496
00:35:02,799 --> 00:35:04,860
I have been green too, Miss Eyre.

497
00:35:05,060 --> 00:35:10,979
I, grass green, not a more vernal tint, freshens you now than once freshened me.

498
00:35:12,209 --> 00:35:17,400
My spring is gone, however, but it has left me that French flowerette on my

499
00:35:17,401 --> 00:35:21,299
hands, which, in some moods, I would feign be rid of.

500
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:28,680
Not valuing now the root once its sprang, having found that it was of a sort which

501
00:35:28,681 --> 00:35:33,840
nothing but gold dust could manure, I have but half a liking to the blossom,

502
00:35:34,959 --> 00:35:38,180
especially when it looks so artificial as just now.

503
00:35:39,459 --> 00:35:43,029
I keep it and rear it rather on the Roman Catholic principle

504
00:35:43,030 --> 00:35:48,799
of expiating numerous sins, great or small, by one good work.
